The csm-calls rollback release (docs/forms/STAGE2-CONTRACT.md 4.7).

Release 2cacdca5 plus three guards, so a rollback leaves the rows Stage 2a writes as they are, but
for the two losses the csm-calls RUNBOOK names (Release / rollback):
  1. the re-match loop skips a stored row with no external invitee (a 2a candidate);
     the release itself makes call rows for external meetings only;
  2. the transcript loop reads each meeting's class with its raw before it takes its 8,
     and fetches client and candidate meetings only, never a stripped sales or internal one;
  3. a Fathom row placed by hand keeps the booking link, the kind and the client name the
     2a manual match wrote: existing() reads them for Fathom rows, and keepManual keeps them
     (the release read no link, so every rerun wrote linked_call_id null and the kind afresh).

Stage it beside the new release <sha8> (hermes/csm-calls/RUNBOOK.md, Release / rollback):
  R=/home/hermes/.csm-calls-releases-hermes
  mkdir -p $R/rollback-<sha8> && tar -x -C $R/rollback-<sha8> -f <git archive 2cacdca5 hermes/csm-calls>
  cd $R/rollback-<sha8> && patch -p1 < $R/<sha8>/hermes/csm-calls/rollback/2cacdca5.patch
Tested by hermes/csm-calls/rollback.test.ts.

